istinct breed from the American Pit Bull Terrier, although they share some ancestral roots. The Staffy is recognized as a separate breed by The Kennel Club and has its specific breed standard, as we mentioned on our homepage."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "<strong><strong>Why do Staffies scratch so much?</strong></strong>", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Excessive scratching in Staffies can be a sign of allergies (food or environmental), skin dryness, parasites (fleas, mites), or even stress. If your Staffy is scratching frequently, it's important to consult with a veterinarian to determine the cause and appropriate treatment."}}]}]};
